21:41:19 [105e] Developmental order (easiest first): what -> who -> where -> when -> why -> how.
21:41:19 [105e] Primary WH types (prefer these): what, who, where.
21:41:19 [105e] Use only with clear support: when.
21:41:19 [105e] Emerging / optional: why, how.
21:41:19 [105e] - WH-questions are appropriate around ages 4-5, but should follow a difficulty hierarchy.
21:41:19 [105e] - Begin with what/who questions, then where, then when, then why/how.
21:41:19 [105e] - Why and how questions should be simple, concrete, and supported by visible evidence or familiar routines.
